# Phase 18 compatibility release gate — execution log

- P18-V01 inherited-trait correction: pinned Java 5.5.1 `ConsumerRunningInfo`,
  `ProcessQueueInfo`, `PopProcessQueueInfo`, and `ConsumeStatus` do not declare
  `equals` or `hashCode`; reflection resolves both to `java.lang.Object`.
  Separately constructed default instances are unequal. Rust had derived
  structural equality for all four corresponding public DTOs. Removed those
  `PartialEq`/`Eq` implementations and added compile-fail rustdoc guards.
- Extended the invoked Java `ConsumerRunningInfoFixtures` with identity and
  declaring-class cases. Rust checks all four cases and compares the decoded
  Consumer Running Info body as normalized JSON values, preserving the wire
  differential without using DTO value equality. Fixture SHA-256:
  `a16ba3fd660aa1b8ad6ef2150163a9657283ada56c728f6769f39f98b0a5fbe8`.
- Updated the Phase 6 API map, Phase 10 method matrix, release checklist, and
  requirement audit. This closes four related inherited-trait discrepancies
  only; broad P18-V01 remains open.
- Verification passed: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-protocol --all-features
  --locked` (all unit, integration, and 20 doctests); strict protocol Clippy;
  `mvn -q -o -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` (37 scenarios, fixture
  drift and Java/Rust cross-decodes); `cargo fmt --all -- --check`; and
  `git diff --check`.
- The full workspace P18-V02 gate still needs rerunning on the revision that
  includes these changes.
